{"title":"Juniper Coffee","sub":"Should we open a coffee kiosk at a busy station?","type":"Investment / capacity","industry":"Food service","geo":"United Kingdom","diff":1,"fmt":"Interviewer-led","time":"25-30 min","skills":"Capacity at peak · break-even · payback","prompt":"Juniper Coffee runs 12 coffee kiosks in the north of England. It has been offered a kiosk on the main concourse of a busy commuter station. The fit-out would cost $120k. The CEO wants to know whether to sign, and what profit to expect.","clarify":[{"q":"How does the station charge rent?","a":"A share of sales: 12% of revenue, with no fixed rent."},{"q":"When are customers there?","a":"Mostly commuters: demand is very concentrated between 7am and 9am on weekdays."},{"q":"Juniper's usual hurdle?","a":"Pay back the fit-out within two years."},{"q":"Staffing?","a":"Two baristas during the morning peak, one for the rest of the day."}],"structure":{"root":"Is the kiosk worth opening?","branches":[{"head":"Revenue","items":["Customers per day: peak vs rest of day","Average spend","Trading days"]},{"head":"Costs","items":["Coffee and food (30% of sales)","Station rent (12% of sales)","Staff and other fixed costs"]},{"head":"Capacity","items":["Drinks a barista can make per hour","Queue length at peak"]}]},"hypothesis":"A station kiosk lives or dies on the morning peak. I'd check whether the kiosk can serve everyone who wants coffee between 7 and 9, not just how many people pass by.","questions":[{"q":"Juniper estimates 300 customers would want coffee in the 7-9am peak and about 90 across the rest of the day. A barista makes about 45 drinks an hour. How many customers can the kiosk actually serve each day?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Peak capacity: 2 baristas × 45 drinks × 2 hours = <b>180</b> drinks. Demand is 300, so <b>120 customers a day walk away</b> (or never join the queue).</p> <p>Daily sales: 180 + 90 = <b>270 customers</b>.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> the kiosk is limited by how fast it can make coffee at peak, not by how many people pass by.</p>"},{"q":"Average spend is $3.80; the kiosk trades 360 days a year. Fixed costs are $110k staff and $15k other. Does it meet the two-year payback?","exhibit":{"kind":"chart","svg":"<svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"400.419875pt\" height=\"193.048pt\" viewBox=\"0 0 400.419875 193.048\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" version=\"1.1\"><defs><style type=\"text/css\">*{stroke-linejoin: round; stroke-linecap: butt}</style></defs><g id=\"figure_1\"><g id=\"patch_1\"><path d=\"M 0 193.048 L 400.419875 193.048 L 400.419875 0 L 0 0 L 0 193.048 z\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/></g><g id=\"axes_1\"><g id=\"patch_2\"><path d=\"M 47.259875 159.456 L 393.219875 159.456 L 393.219875 9.768 L 47.259875 9.768 L 47.259875 159.456 z\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/></g><g id=\"matplotlib.axis_1\"><g id=\"xtick_1\"><g id=\"line2d_1\"><defs><path id=\"mff7d576334\" d=\"M 0 0 L 0 3.5 \" style=\"stroke: #555555; stroke-width: 0.8\"/></defs><g><use xlink:href=\"#mff7d576334\" x=\"79.834031\" y=\"159.456\" style=\"fill: #555555; stroke: #555555; stroke-width: 0.8\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_1\"><g style=\"fill: #555555\" transform=\"translate(63.554031 174.184) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-2d\" d=\"M 4013 122 Q 4032 77 4009 38 Q 3987 0 3942 0 L 3475 0 Q 3405 0 3373 77 L 2547 2093 Q 2515 2163 2394 2163 L 1312 2163 Q 1267 2163 1251 2144 Q 1235 2125 1235 2093 L 1235 102 Q 1235 0 1126 0 L 710 0 Q 659 0 640 22 Q 621 45 621 83 L 621 4659 Q 621 4749 698 4749 L 2483 4749 Q 3238 4749 3657 4438 Q 4077 4128 4077 3520 Q 4077 3155 3936 2902 Q 3795 2650 3580 2499 Q 3366 2349 3142 2278 Q 3091 2272 3117 2214 L 4013 122 L 4013 122 z\nM 2304 2611 Q 2867 2611 3152 2816 Q 3437 3021 3437 3462 Q 3437 3891 3184 4096 Q 2931 4301 2451 4301 L 1325 4301 Q 1235 4301 1235 4230 L 1235 2694 Q 1235 2611 1293 2611 L 2304 2611 L 2304 2611 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-48\" d=\"M 851 1485 Q 851 117