nsform=\"translate(55.703125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-84\" transform=\"translate(120.609375 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_19\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(239.621044 74.8032) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-e3\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\" transform=\"translate(55.703125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\" transform=\"translate(102.203125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-80\" transform=\"translate(148.703125 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_20\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(297.779006 117.25934) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-e3\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\" transform=\"translate(55.703125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-85\" transform=\"translate(102.203125 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_21\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(355.341969 123.048814) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-88\" d=\"M 2131 4813 Q 2598 4813 2950 4649 Q 3302 4486 3500 4192 Q 3699 3898 3699 3507 Q 3699 3206 3545 2969 Q 3392 2733 3053 2496 Q 2957 2432 3046 2394 Q 3341 2278 3529 2112 Q 3718 1946 3814 1731 Q 3910 1517 3910 1261 Q 3910 858 3683 557 Q 3456 256 3053 96 Q 2650 -64 2112 -64 Q 1587 -64 1196 83 Q 806 230 598 508 Q 390 787 390 1178 Q 390 1517 560 1789 Q 730 2061 1120 2304 Q 1197 2349 1200 2377 Q 1203 2406 1126 2445 Q 947 2547 809 2688 Q 672 2829 595 3014 Q 518 3200 518 3437 Q 518 3827 720 4137 Q 922 4448 1286 4630 Q 1651 4813 2131 4813 L 2131 4813 z\nM 2138 4365 Q 1850 4365 1613 4249 Q 1376 4134 1238 3939 Q 1101 3744 1101 3488 Q 1101 2906 1760 2758 L 2419 2605 Q 2509 2579 2633 2649 Q 2758 2720 2880 2854 Q 3002 2989 3078 3161 Q 3155 3334 3155 3514 Q 3155 3891 2880 4128 Q 2605 4365 2138 4365 L 2138 4365 z\nM 2144 384 Q 2675 384 2988 614 Q 3302 845 3302 1235 Q 3302 1530 3142 1715 Q 2982 1901 2624 1984 L 1792 2189 Q 1696 2214 1555 2153 Q 1414 2093 1273 1961 Q 1133 1830 1033 1648 Q 934 1466 934 1248 Q 934 838 1244 611 Q 1555 384 2144 384 L 2144 384 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-88\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-89\" transform=\"translate(66.796875 0)\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"pbc4b9f4aee\"><rect x=\"47.259875\" y=\"9.768\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"149.688\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · Kiosk economics, year one ($k)","note":null},"answer":"<p>Revenue: 270 × $3.80 × 360 = <b>$369k</b>.</p> <p>Margin after coffee and station rent: 100% − 30% − 12% = 58%, so contribution = $214k.</p> <p>Profit: $214k − $125k = <b>$89k</b>. Payback: $120k ÷ $89k = <b>1.3 years</b>. It meets the hurdle.</p> <p>Break-even: $125k ÷ ($3.80 × 58% × 360) ≈ <b>158 customers a day</b>, versus 270 expected: a comfortable cushion.</p>"},{"q":"A third barista for the morning peak would cost about $15k a year. Worth it?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Peak capacity rises to 3 × 45 × 2 = 270, still short of the 300 who want coffee, but +90 customers a day (30 are still turned away).</p> <p>Extra profit: 90 × $3.80 × 58% × 360 − $15k = <b>$56k a year</b>.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> yes, clearly. Also add app pre-ordering so regulars skip the queue, and check the kiosk layout can fit a third person and a second machine.</p>"}],"reco":"Sign the lease. The kiosk should make about $89k a year and pay back the $120k fit-out in 1.3 years, with break-even at about 158 customers a day versus 270 expected. But the real constraint is the morning peak: with two baristas, 120 customers a day can't be served. Adding a third barista at peak adds about $56k a year. Risk: commuter numbers fall if hybrid working grows, so negotiate a break clause. Next step: confirm the kiosk can fit a second coffee machine.","great":["Checks peak capacity before revenue","Treats station rent as a share of sales, not a fixed cost","Computes break-even and the safety margin","Sees that adding peak capacity is the biggest lever"],"id":31,"slug":"juniper-coffee"}